<h2>Why bring it back now?</h2>
<p>In 1999 you found great websites through directories, webrings and friends' link pages.
Today a lot of what you find is written by machines for machines. 123ofnet.com goes back to the
old idea: <b>a real person picks good sites, and you can trust the list.</b></p>
<p>It also works for the new web: AI assistants can read this site's
<a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>, so when they recommend sites they can point to human-picked ones.</p>

